[
    RuntimeEnabled=DomicileControlChannel,
    Exposed=Window
] interface DomicileLockedEvent : Event {
  constructor(DOMString type,
              optional DomicileLockedEventInit eventInitDict = {});

  // Whether this desk is locked: true is a desktop that will not deliver a
  // keystroke or a click to any client until somebody says the passphrase.
  //
  // THE COMPOSITOR HOLDS IT, AND NOTHING IN THIS RENDERER CAN CHANGE IT. Input
  // on this system does not originate in the compositor -- the shell's page
  // owns it and forwards it, and the compositor injects it into a Wayland seat
  // -- so the lock is the injection not happening. That is why a page reload
  // does not open the desk, why an engine that died and came back does not, and
  // why a page edited in the devtools of the browser drawing it does not
  // either.
  //
  // THE PAGE KEEPS ITS OWN KEYS while this is true, which reads like a hole and
  // is the opposite: the page is the thing forwarding, so it can draw a lock
  // screen and take a passphrase while nothing it forwards reaches a client.
  // DomicileHost.unlock() is how it offers one.
  //
  // A state rather than an edge, and sent again to a page that has only just
  // connected -- see DomicileIdleEvent.idle, which says why that is the shape
  // the wire needs. Here it is also the point: the edge a reloaded page missed
  // is the one that would have raised its lock screen.
  readonly attribute boolean locked;

  // When the browser process had this message, on `performance.now()`'s clock.
  // See DomicileModifiersEvent.arrival for what this is and what it is not.
  readonly attribute DOMHighResTimeStamp arrival;
};
